+<a id="ARCH-DATAFLOW-001"></a>
+
+### ARCH-DATAFLOW-001 — Scheduled write path and precomputed read path
+
+The hourly weather flow is the only weather write path:
+
+```text
+Cron Trigger (hourly)
+  1. acquire D1 lock for "weather-sync" with a 15-minute expiry; abort if held
+  2. create a running sync run for the primary provider
+  3. fetch bounded city batches; on primary exhaustion, try the configured fallback
+  4. validate provider DTOs and normalize them to internal types
+  5. record each failed city and continue with valid cities
+  6. transactionally persist pending snapshot, daily, hourly, score, and ranking rows in D1
+  7. fully validate the complete candidate in D1; mark it failed and stop publication on any error
+  8. write and checksum-verify immutable, undiscoverable, snapshot-scoped KV read models
+  9. in one D1 transaction revalidate the candidate, activate its D1 pointer, and supersede the old snapshot
+ 10. after the D1 commit, update the small `v1:manifest:active` KV manifest pointer
+ 11. mark the run successful or partial
+ 12. release the owner-aware D1 lock
+```
+
+Step 8 writes only high-entropy `snapshotId` keys that have never appeared in a manifest, response, log, or public URL. It does not overwrite an active key. The candidate becomes discoverable only through step 10, after full validation, immutable-key read-back verification, and the D1 activation commit have succeeded.
+
+Every user request follows the read-only path:
+
+```text
+User request
+  → Cloudflare CDN / Next.js route or Server Component
+  → application use case
+  → read the small `v1:manifest:active` KV pointer
+  → read the referenced immutable snapshot-scoped KV model
+  → on manifest miss/error or referenced-key miss/mismatch, query only the D1 active pointer and rows
+  → on unavailable trustworthy data, return deployed static content or a typed unavailable result
+  → ViewModel → HTML or JSON
+
+User request ─X→ Open-Meteo / WeatherAPI
+```
+
+An edge that still sees the old manifest can safely read the old immutable, previously validated snapshot until KV propagation completes; the response exposes its real freshness. A missing or malformed manifest, or a missing/checksum-mismatched key referenced by a manifest, falls back only to the D1 active pointer and its rows. That path never guesses a snapshot ID, lists KV, probes a pending candidate, or searches arbitrary old KV keys. If D1 is also unavailable, it returns deployed static content or an explicit unavailable outcome rather than discovering another snapshot.
+
+The read path never writes a weather read model, computes a score, or contacts a provider. D1 and its active pointer are authoritative; KV contains immutable compact read models plus one replaceable manifest pointer.
+
+Roadmap: [REL-MVP-ARCH_DATAFLOW_001](11-Roadmap.md#REL-MVP-ARCH_DATAFLOW_001).
+
+#### Acceptance Criteria
+
+- An integration test observes zero provider calls for every public page and read-API use case, including cache misses.
+- A successful Cron run persists pending D1 data, fully validates it, writes and verifies undiscoverable immutable KV keys, activates the D1 pointer transactionally, and only then updates the KV manifest, in exactly that order.
+- A failed city is isolated and recorded while valid cities in the bounded batch remain eligible for publication.
+- An old manifest resolves only a previously validated immutable snapshot; a manifest or referenced-key miss resolves only the D1 active snapshot and never a pending or guessed KV key.
+- Failure before D1 activation leaves both pointers unchanged; failure after D1 activation but before manifest update leaves the old KV pointer safe while D1 already identifies the new active snapshot.
+- Only an activated, fully validated snapshot can become the basis of a discoverable public ranking or read model.
+
