+<a id="ARCH-RECOVERY-001"></a>
+
+### ARCH-RECOVERY-001 — Last-known-good activation and degraded reads
+
+A D1 conditional lock row with holder, acquisition time, and expiry prevents overlapping Cron runs. The default `weather-sync` lock expires after 15 minutes so a crashed holder cannot block future runs indefinitely; release is owner-aware, and a second run aborts rather than proceeding concurrently.
+
+A candidate snapshot remains pending while normalized weather, scores, and rankings are completed in D1. Full candidate validation runs before any KV write. After it passes, the publisher writes all candidate models to new immutable high-entropy snapshot keys and verifies their checksums by read-back. It then executes one D1 transaction that locks and revalidates the pending candidate, changes the previous active snapshot to `superseded`, changes the candidate to `active`, and updates the singleton D1 active-snapshot pointer. A conflict or failed revalidation rolls back the entire transaction.
+
+Only after that D1 commit may the publisher replace `v1:manifest:active` with the new snapshot ID and model version. Failure before the D1 commit leaves the old D1 and KV pointers unchanged. Failure between the D1 commit and manifest replacement leaves an old KV pointer that still references immutable validated data; manifest or new-key misses fall back only to the new D1 active pointer. Orphan candidate keys are not discoverable and are later garbage-collected after the rollback window. A partial or corrupt candidate never replaces the previous active snapshot. Per-city failures are recorded and do not roll back unrelated valid city writes, but the complete publishable candidate must still pass the declared coverage threshold.
+
+Provider failure preserves the previous active snapshot. A valid old manifest may continue serving its immutable last-known-good value with `stale: true` and its real `dataUpdatedAt`. A manifest miss/error or referenced-key miss/mismatch falls back only to D1 active data; if that D1 read also fails, the resolver uses deployed static content or returns a typed unavailable outcome, never an arbitrary KV snapshot. No degraded result is described as live, and no user path contacts a provider.
+
+Roadmap: [REL-MVP-ARCH_RECOVERY_001](11-Roadmap.md#REL-MVP-ARCH_RECOVERY_001).
+
+#### Acceptance Criteria
+
+- Concurrent-run tests allow only one unexpired D1 lock holder and prove that an expired crashed lock can be recovered.
+- Fault-injection tests prove that invalid or incompletely published candidates change neither pointer and remain undiscoverable.
+- Transaction tests prove that D1 status changes and the singleton active pointer commit atomically, while the KV manifest update occurs only after commit.
+- Provider, manifest, immutable-key, D1, and partial-city failure tests produce the documented degraded outcome without a user-path provider call or arbitrary old-key lookup.
+- Stale results preserve previously validated immutable data, set `stale: true`, and expose the original update time and snapshot ID.
+- Absence of trustworthy manifest-resolved, D1-active, or deployed static data produces a typed unavailable outcome, not fabricated data.
+
